---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About" description="About FAMENL · FAIR Metadata Exchange Netherlands.">
  <section>
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="section-label">About</div>
      <h1 class="section-title">About FAMENL</h1>
      <p class="section-lead">
        FAMENL (FAIR Metadata Exchange Netherlands) is a collaborative initiative that builds shared
        metadata infrastructure for Dutch life science research infrastructures.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;margin:2rem 0 .75rem;">The Problem</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        Life science research infrastructures in the Netherlands each operate with their own data management
        systems tailored to specific domains, bioimaging, omics, stem cell research, environmental monitoring.
        These systems cannot speak to each other. Metadata produced in one domain is invisible to another,
        making cross-disciplinary data reuse and integration unnecessarily difficult.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;margin:2rem 0 .75rem;">Our Approach</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem;">
        FAMENL develops FAIR metadata management layers that sit between domain-specific platforms and generic
        storage solutions. Rather than replacing existing tools, we build bridges: using the ISA standard to
        describe dataset relationships, deploying FAIRDOM-SEEK as a unified user-facing interface, and packaging
        research outputs as Digital Research Objects in RO-Crate format.
      </p>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        A key principle is accessibility. FAMENL delivers simple, tabular metadata templates so that individual
        researchers can produce standards-compliant data without requiring deep technical expertise.
      </p>

      <blockquote style="border-left:4px solid #52b788;background:#d8f3dc;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-family:'Lora',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.05rem;color:#2d6a4f;margin:2rem 0;">
        "Simple, tabular data templates, empowering individuals to produce data compliant with community
        metadata standards without requiring technical expertise."
      </blockquote>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;margin:2rem 0 .75rem;">Key Technologies</h2>
      <ul style="color:var(--muted);padding-left:1.5rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">ISA framework</strong>: describes the relationships between investigations, studies, and assays across domains</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">FAIRDOM-SEEK</strong>: unified frontend with multi-level access permissions across infrastructure boundaries</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">RO-Crate</strong>: packages datasets and metadata as portable Digital Research Objects</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">REMBI</strong>: bioimaging metadata standard for microscopy</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;margin:2rem 0 .75rem;">Relation to prepFAME</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);">
        prepFAME was a 12-month preparatory project that mapped existing metadata standards and requirements
        across Dutch life science research infrastructures. Its findings directly informed the design and
        scope of FAMENL.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
